    name: 'Expedition Dinosaur',
    title: 'Expedition Dinosaur',
    description:
      'Travel back in time with Expedition: Dinosaur, the most fun you’ve had in the last 75 million years! Coming to the Science Spectrum from February 15 through June 1, 2025, this thrilling exhibition features life-like animatronic dinosaurs, engaging hands-on interactives, and educational displays that immerse guests in the prehistoric world. Walk among realistic robotic dinosaurs like the Albertosaurus, Velociraptors, Stegosaurus, Triceratops, and more—brought to life with special effects and sounds. Become a paleontologist by exploring excavation artifacts, interactive fossils, an augmented reality sandbox, and even a dinosaur egg incubator challenge. Solve puzzles, reassemble Pangea, and enjoy dinosaur rubbings to take home. Learn how tails move, gizzards work, eggs hatch, and how dinosaurs battled head-to-head. Don’t miss the epic T-Rex head photo-op for a unique souvenir! The OMNI Theater will also show Dinosaurs: Giants of Patagonia from February 14 to June 1. Find showtimes, trailers, and pricing at sciencespectrum.org. The exhibition is located in the Exhibit Hall and open during regular museum hours. Expedition: Dinosaur pricing is $14.50 adults / $12 children & seniors (exhibit with museum OR film), and $20 adults / $17 children & seniors (exhibit with museum AND film). Special group rates and guided tours are available. Created by Stage Nine Design and distributed by Exhibits Development Group.',
