    timezone: 'CDT',
    description:
      'Travel back in time with a trolley tour through the National Ranching Heritage Center’s 19-acre historical park, where 55 authentic ranching structures dating from the 1780s to the 1950s tell the story of America’s ranching legacy. Running from April 9 through May 31 (weather permitting), tours take place Wednesdays through Sundays, with multiple time slots available. Each 45-minute tour is free, and reservations can be made at the front desk upon arrival. Seating is limited to 21 guests per tour. These educational and immersive tours are made possible by The CH Foundation, which donated the trolley. For more information, visit [ranchingheritage.org](https://ranchingheritage.org) or call (806) 742-0498.',
